   "subject": "Updating package dependency",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I am developping a R package on github. It now is version 1.0, previous version was 0.1.<br></div><div><br></div><div>I deployed a Shiny app on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792362598808000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0zNZLkpa91lr7hVJZ_9WUj\">shinyapps.io</a> using version 0.1. Then I updated the package and now want the app to work with version 1.0. I have tried deleting the app, changing package name, etc., but it still works with the old version. I know it because the new version should support a given type of file input that gives an error with the app, which it wouldn&#39;t if the right package version were installed.</div><div><br></div><div>Has anyone experienced similar issues? How to update an app dependency?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks a lot, best wishes</div><div><br></div><div>Maëlle.</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
