   "date": "2015-11-28T15:30:14Z",
   "subject": "Re: [shinyapps-users] Updating package dependency",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Apologies, we have Thanksgiving this week so most of us are offline.<div><br></div><div>Can you do me a favor and do a few things:</div><div>0. Capture the output of shinyapps::appDependencies()</div><div>1. Upgrade to the latest version of the shinyapps package.</div><div>2. Confirm that the output of shinyapps::appDependencies() is picking up the right version of your package.</div><div>3. Deploy again if the output of step 0 and Step 2 are different.</div><div><br></div><div>Also, which version of the IDE are you running with?</div><div>-Tareef</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Nov 26, 2015 at 11:12 AM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">maelle....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I did this again (checking the session info and that the app was working) and then I typed deployApp() again but the app is still not using the right version of the package. Thanks for helping.<span><br><br>On Thursday, November 26, 2015 at 4:32:01 PM UTC+1, Tareef Kawaf wrote:</span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span>I am assuming all you need to do is install it using devotions::install_github. <div>I would run library() of your library and then run sessionInfo() to make sure it picked up the new version, run the application locally<span></span> before you deploy again.  </div></span></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div><br><br>On Thursday, November 26, 2015,  &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">maelle....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Yes, thanks, but I have installed the package again from github right before I deployed the app. Is there a particular way of doing it?<br><br>On Thursday, November 26, 2015 at 3:36:58 PM UTC+1, Tareef Kawaf wrote:</div></blockquote></div></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">You need to install the package again for your application locally and then redeploy the application.  <div>Hth </div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div>Tareef<br><br>On Thursday, November 26, 2015,  &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">maelle....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I am developping a R package on github. It now is version 1.0, previous version was 0.1.<br></div><div><br></div><div>I deployed a Shiny app on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792362598818000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0LMZBOed7jGJb81IX3_EuG\">shinyapps.io</a> using version 0.1. Then I updated the package and now want the app to work with version 1.0. I have tried deleting the app, changing package name, etc., but it still works with the old version. I know it because the new version should support a given type of file input that gives an error with the app, which it wouldn&#39;t if the right package version were installed.</div><div><br></div><div>Has anyone experienced similar issues? How to update an app dependency?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks a lot, best wishes</div><div><br></div><div>Maëlle.</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ShinyApps Users&quot; group.<br></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
